The '''Centre Financer Internacional''' ({{lang|ca|Centre Financer Internacional}}; "International Financial Centre") is a 60-storey office tower at 200 [[Avinguda Embarcadero]] in the [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]] of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. At 265 metres (869 ft) in architectural height, it is among the tallest buildings in [[Balboa]]. The tower was completed in 1988 during the [[Balboa real-estate bubble|real-estate bubble]] and is one of the most visible symbols of that era of speculative construction.

The building was developed by [[Grup de Construcció Balboa]], a real estate development company that collapsed in the [[Balboa real-estate bubble|real-estate crisis]] of 1991. The tower itself survived the crisis intact and was acquired by [[Grup Ciutat Nova]] in the late 1990s. It operates as a multi-tenant office building, housing financial services firms, law firms, and corporate tenants associated with the [[Balboa Canal|canal corridor]] economy.

== Architecture ==

The Centre Financer Internacional has a broad rectangular massing divided into two closely connected vertical wings. Its façade is a blue-green glass curtain wall with closely spaced metallic fins, giving the tower a strong vertical emphasis. The upper section has a stepped, twin-crown profile with taller mechanical and screened rooftop zones that distinguish the two wings on the skyline.

A darker technical and transfer-floor band runs around the middle-lower portion of the tower, breaking the curtain wall into visually distinct zones and housing mechanical plant, elevator transfer levels, and service floors. The lower levels connect visually to the historic waterfront complex, although the tower maintains its own lobby, service access, loading area, and structural core.

The building's footprint is approximately 2,000 to 2,400 m², roughly comparable to a rectangle measuring 52 by 42 metres. The tower uses two linked cores serving separate elevator zones, with a typical usable office floor of approximately 1,400 to 1,700 m² after subtracting the central core, elevators, stairs, washrooms, mechanical shafts, and structural areas.

