=== Floor arrangement ===

The lower four to six tower floors contain the main lobby, conference facilities, restaurants, retail, and building services. Above that are approximately 45 to 50 regular office floors, several mechanical or transfer floors, and executive offices near the top. The building's wide shape accommodates two linked cores or a large central core serving separate elevator zones for low-rise, mid-rise, and high-rise tenant access.

== History ==

=== Construction and the real-estate bubble ===

The Centre Financer Internacional was developed by [[Grup de Construcció Balboa]], a real estate development company active during the [[Balboa real-estate bubble|real-estate bubble]] of the mid-1980s. Construction began in 1985 and the tower was completed in 1988. At 265 metres, it became the most prominent addition to the Sant Cristòfor waterfront skyline.

The tower was conceived as a speculative multi-tenant office building, intended to capitalise on the demand for premium office space from financial services firms, canal corridor companies, and foreign businesses establishing offices in Sant Cristòfor during the bubble. Its location at 200 Avinguda Embarcadero placed it at the centre of the [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]], directly on the waterfront boulevard.

=== Post-crisis ===

[[Grup de Construcció Balboa]] collapsed in the real-estate crisis of 1991, along with many of the bubble-era developers. Unlike the [[Banc Balboa Tower]], which was damaged by a fire during the crisis and required refurbishment, the Centre Financer Internacional survived the downturn intact. The building's tenant base — diversified across financial services, law firms, and corporate tenants rather than dependent on a single institution — provided more stable occupancy than the single-tenant towers that had been built during the same period.

The tower was acquired by [[Grup Ciutat Nova]] in the late 1990s as part of the company's early expansion into office tower ownership. Under Grup Ciutat Nova's ownership, the building has been maintained and upgraded, with periodic renovations to the mechanical systems, lobby, and common areas. The tower remains one of the most prestigious office addresses in Sant Cristòfor and is fully occupied.

== Tenants ==

The Centre Financer Internacional operates as a multi-tenant office building. Its tenant base includes financial services firms, energy companies, and industrial corporations associated with the [[Balboa Canal|canal corridor]] economy. The building's large floor plates and dual-core configuration allow tenants to lease contiguous floors or half-floors, accommodating both large institutional tenants and smaller professional firms.

