== In popular culture ==

The Centre Financer Internacional is one of the most recognisable buildings on the Sant Cristòfor waterfront skyline. Its blue-green curtain wall and twin-crown profile make it a frequent subject of photographs and postcards of the city. The tower's association with the real-estate bubble — and its survival of the crisis that destroyed its developer — has made it a subject of commentary on the boom-and-bust cycle of the Balboan economy.

